docs/sol/sol_round3.out:800:| 2. Release service owns release facts | **Addressed only in words** | “Verdicts, approvals, evidence provenance, and released status are written only by the release service” carries the requirement ([release facts](/Users/user/code-projects/chief-command/docs/ARCHITECTURE_v2_2026-07-14.md:152)). But the harness submits “authenticated observations.” If the whole harness shares one submitting identity, a compromised harness can submit false reviewer and test observations, and the release service will faithfully turn them into trusted facts. Sole writing does not establish truth. The phrase “or a release-account process” also opens an undefined second writer. |
docs/sol/sol_round3.out:904:- **GitHub itself:** Administrator bypass, automation identities, package publishing, release creation, environment approvals and third-party GitHub applications may provide alternate authority.
docs/sol/sol_round3.out:910:- **Backup and restoration:** Restoring old configuration can revive old credentials, stale approvals, unsafe automation or a vulnerable release path.
docs/sol/sol_round3.out:912:Production must reject anything not signed by the sole approved chain. Merely saying “all releases should use this service” is not enough.
docs/sol/sol_round3.out:926:- Social engineering that persuades Neill to paste a secret, mount a folder or approve a system dialog.
