docs/sol/sol_round4.out:6056:The live record has a serious drift problem. The written rules were strengthened, but the existing database kept older versions because startup only creates missing rules; it does not replace outdated ones. In the live record, a failing verdict can still be deleted, and the “full panel” check can count a tester as if it were an independent reviewer. The one recorded “shipped” job also has no run identifier, branch, working copy, or exact code version attached. So the document’s claim that the audit protections are “already built and regression-tested” is too strong.
