    40	nobody reviewed and one where a broken login would have permanently condemned good code.
    41	All fixed with regression tests.
    42	
    43	### #11 — the gatekeeper (built, NOT pushed, `66ad8a2`)
    44	
    45	`harness/gatekeeper.py`. Three verbs — merge, deploy, spend — and no fourth. Agents ask;
    46	it re-reads the record itself rather than believing the request. `dispatch.ship()`, which
    47	was one import away from every agent, is gone.
    48	
    49	Reviewers hit it hard and found more, all fixed — most seriously that **merge merged
    50	whatever the branch currently pointed at, never checking it was the code that had been
    51	reviewed**. Build v1, get it approved, push v2, ask to merge: v2 went in. It now refuses
    52	unless the branch tip *is* the reviewed version, and the record decides before git is
    53	touched at all.
